       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg. A dose this high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema, and in overdose it can cause prolonged shock. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that limit.\n\nIt may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the standard starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for a frail or elderly patient, or one on other antihypertensives\n\nIf 50 mg is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
