       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one as written. No standard indication supports amlodipine 50 mg daily, and amlodipine accumulates because its half-life is 30 to 50 hours. Daily dosing at five times the maximum could cause serious hypotension and shock. You haven't given a clinical rationale, and a confirmation alone doesn't resolve the safety concern.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Change the dose:** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily right away. If the blood pressure needs more control, adding a second agent is the usual approach, not going above 10 mg.\n- **Talk to pharmacy:** If you have a specific reason for this dose, a pharmacist or attending can co-review it. If they approve it, it can be entered through a pathway with that documented override.\n- **Check the order:** If it was meant to be a different drug or a different unit, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order."
      }
